WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:15.520
Lemonade Detectives hurried back outside.

2
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.283
Henry scanned the crowd, looking for the mysterious woman.

3
00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:23.126
He spotted some shiny green fabric and stepped forward.

4
00:00:24.027 --> 00:00:24.748
Then he stopped.

5
00:00:25.328 --> 00:00:27.130
It was just a man wearing a green shirt.

6
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.712
"I don't see her," Cole said.

7
00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:32.121
Henry sighed.

8
00:00:32.141 --> 00:00:33.482
"Me neither.

9
00:00:34.263 --> 00:00:36.184
It's hard to see anything in this crowd."

10
00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:39.867
"We need to figure out where she went," Maggie declared.

11
00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:43.049
"Because she was definitely acting suspicious!"

12
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.511
"You're right," Cole said.

13
00:00:45.531 --> 00:00:49.233
"But why would a stranger steal Nathan's painting?"

14
00:00:50.374 --> 00:00:52.116
Henry was wondering the same thing.

15
00:00:52.136 --> 00:00:54.677
"It doesn't make sense," he said.

16
00:00:55.578 --> 00:00:56.399
Maggie frowned.

17
00:00:56.419 --> 00:01:01.290
"I told you, that woman is probably an international art thief.

18
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.892
Anyway, why would she run unless she's guilty?"

19
00:01:04.912 --> 00:01:06.613
"I don't know."

20
00:01:07.413 --> 00:01:08.494
Henry checked his phone.

21
00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:11.856
"We only have thirty minutes until the judging starts.

22
00:01:12.877 --> 00:01:15.418
We need to keep investigating all our suspects."

23
00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:17.159
Cole nodded.

24
00:01:17.179 --> 00:01:19.701
"We can watch for that woman along the way."

25
00:01:19.721 --> 00:01:21.582
"Let's ask Mrs.

26
00:01:21.642 --> 00:01:22.503
Sweet about Mr.

27
00:01:22.543 --> 00:01:24.524
Collins' alibi," Henry said.

28
00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:29.928
"After talking with her, we might be able to cross one suspect off the list."

29
00:01:31.069 --> 00:01:32.470
They headed to the crafts fair.

30
00:01:35.072 --> 00:01:36.393
It was easy to spot Mrs.

31
00:01:36.453 --> 00:01:39.496
Sweet's booth by the long line near the free candy samples.

32
00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:41.418
"Hi, kids.

33
00:01:41.658 --> 00:01:43.099
How's the lemonade business?"

34
00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:44.420
Mrs. Sweet asked.

35
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.862
"Great," Maggie said.

36
00:01:46.882 --> 00:01:49.264
"Good!" Mrs.

37
00:01:49.324 --> 00:01:50.225
Sweet beamed at them.

38
00:01:50.245 --> 00:01:53.428
"Did you come to sign up for my candy class?

39
00:01:54.368 --> 00:01:57.230
The next one starts right after the art show judging."

40
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.852
"Maybe," Henry said.

41
00:01:59.872 --> 00:02:02.995
"Actually, we were wondering something.

42
00:02:03.655 --> 00:02:04.296
Was Mr.

43
00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:06.397
Collins here for your last class?"

44
00:02:07.518 --> 00:02:08.218
"Oh yes."

45
00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:10.020
Mrs. Sweet chuckled.

46
00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.262
"I think that man ate more candy than he made!

47
00:02:14.923 --> 00:02:19.187
I had to chase him away after the class ended so I could clean up for the next

48
00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:31.191
class." "Okay, that's one suspect off the list," Cole said as The Lemonade Detectives left the candy booth.

49
00:02:31.211 --> 00:02:32.552
"Who's left?"

50
00:02:33.572 --> 00:02:35.253
Maggie ticked them off on her fingers.

51
00:02:35.273 --> 00:02:39.675
"Sunglasses woman, Nora, Hannah, and Patrick."

52
00:02:40.795 --> 00:02:43.557
"Let's try to find Patrick first," Henry said.

53
00:02:43.577 --> 00:02:48.039
"It's kind of suspicious that he didn't meet Owen when he was supposed to."

54
00:02:49.199 --> 00:02:50.620
"True," Cole agreed.

55
00:02:51.664 --> 00:02:56.127
"Maybe he was late because he was busy hiding Nathan's painting in the bushes somewhere."

56
00:02:57.048 --> 00:02:58.629
They headed back toward the art show.

57
00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:03.632
Halfway there they spotted Patrick and Owen standing in line at the burger stand.

58
00:03:03.652 --> 00:03:07.055
"We've been looking for you," Henry told Patrick.

59
00:03:07.075 --> 00:03:09.036
"Join the club."

60
00:03:09.736 --> 00:03:10.477
Owen laughed.

61
00:03:10.977 --> 00:03:12.258
He didn't seem annoyed anymore.

62
00:03:12.278 --> 00:03:14.880
"You found me," Patrick said.

63
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.001
"What's up?"

64
00:03:16.921 --> 00:03:18.482
"Did you hear about Nathan's painting?"

65
00:03:18.702 --> 00:03:19.483
Cole asked.

66
00:03:19.503 --> 00:03:20.904
"It's missing."

67
00:03:21.876 --> 00:03:22.757
"Yeah, I heard."

68
00:03:23.337 --> 00:03:24.858
Patrick didn't look very upset.

69
00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:28.781
"So?" "So where have you been for the past hour?"

70
00:03:29.061 --> 00:03:29.962
Maggie blurted out.

71
00:03:30.882 --> 00:03:31.783
Owen laughed again.

72
00:03:31.803 --> 00:03:34.184
"Hey, dude," he told Patrick.

73
00:03:35.105 --> 00:03:35.946
"They're detectives.

74
00:03:36.646 --> 00:03:38.047
They must think you stole it!"

75
00:03:39.028 --> 00:03:40.128
Patrick's eyes narrowed.

76
00:03:40.148 --> 00:03:42.110
"It wasn't me," he said.

77
00:03:42.130 --> 00:03:45.152
"Why would I want a dumb cat painting?

78
00:03:46.193 --> 00:03:48.334
Anyway, I was in the basket-weaving booth.

79
00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.116
You can ask Hannah if you don't believe me."

80
00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.460
"Okay," Henry said.

81
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.241
"Thanks for talking to us."

82
00:03:56.401 --> 00:03:57.862
He led Cole and Maggie away.

83
00:03:57.882 --> 00:04:00.702
"Another alibi," Cole said.

84
00:04:00.722 --> 00:04:03.523
"I guess we can cross Patrick off the list too."

85
00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.264
"I guess so."

86
00:04:05.924 --> 00:04:06.664
Henry shrugged.

87
00:04:07.384 --> 00:04:09.885
"We can double-check his alibi when we talk to Hannah."

88
00:04:10.985 --> 00:04:12.726
Soon they reached the basket-weaving booth.

89
00:04:13.766 --> 00:04:15.647
Hannah was arranging baskets on a shelf.

90
00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:18.007
"Hi," Henry said.

91
00:04:18.027 --> 00:04:20.188
"We were just talking to Patrick.

92
00:04:20.848 --> 00:04:22.569
He said he was over here earlier."

93
00:04:22.589 --> 00:04:26.011
"Yeah." Hannah straightened a large blue basket.

94
00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:29.193
"He wanted me to teach him how to weave a basket."

95
00:04:30.354 --> 00:04:31.634
"Really?" Cole asked.

96
00:04:31.654 --> 00:04:34.656
"You mean he actually wove one himself?"

97
00:04:35.697 --> 00:04:36.437
Hannah nodded.

98
00:04:36.457 --> 00:04:38.959
"He did a pretty good job for a beginner.

99
00:04:39.739 --> 00:04:41.440
You can see for yourself if you want."

100
00:04:42.361 --> 00:04:45.422
She gestured toward a large shopping bag in the back of the booth.

101
00:04:46.523 --> 00:04:47.984
"His basket is in that bag.

102
00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:52.089
He wanted to leave it here so he wouldn't have to carry it around all day."

103
00:04:52.109 --> 00:04:53.950
"That's okay.

104
00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.171
We don't need to see it."

105
00:04:57.131 --> 00:04:58.592
Henry led the way out of the booth.

106
00:04:58.612 --> 00:05:01.693
"I just realized something," Maggie said.

107
00:05:01.713 --> 00:05:04.434
"Hannah is Patrick's alibi, right?

108
00:05:05.095 --> 00:05:07.195
That means Patrick is Hannah's alibi too.

109
00:05:08.336 --> 00:05:10.217
They were together when the painting disappeared."

110
00:05:10.237 --> 00:05:15.099
"So that's two names off the suspect list," Henry said.

111
00:05:15.119 --> 00:05:18.100
"Wait, I just thought of something else."

112
00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:19.481
Maggie frowned.

113
00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:22.702
"What if Hannah and Patrick are covering for each other?

114
00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.323
They could be in cahoots."

115
00:05:25.484 --> 00:05:26.945
"I doubt it," Cole said.

116
00:05:26.965 --> 00:05:29.326
"They don't know each other that well.

117
00:05:29.967 --> 00:05:31.528
They're not even in the same grade."

118
00:05:31.548 --> 00:05:34.810
"You're probably right," Maggie said.

119
00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:38.071
"I still think the weird woman with the sunglasses did it.

120
00:05:38.992 --> 00:05:40.833
Why else would she run away from us like that?"

121
00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:42.754
Henry bit his lip.

122
00:05:42.774 --> 00:05:45.576
"I still don't know what her motive could be.

123
00:05:46.464 --> 00:05:49.067
But I guess she's our only suspect left."

124
00:05:50.128 --> 00:05:53.753
Suddenly he noticed Nora tiptoeing past them, looking rather guilty.

125
00:05:53.773 --> 00:05:56.496
"Well, except for one."
